# On-Prem RAG server — REST Client scratchpad (VS Code "REST Client" extension).
#
# Usage:
#   1. Run "POST /auth/login" first (it's tagged `@name login`).
#   2. Every protected request reuses its JWT via {{login.response.body.$.token}},
#      so you don't paste tokens by hand — just keep the login response in the session.
#   3. Click "Send Request" above any request below.
#
# All routes except /auth/login and /health require `Authorization: Bearer <jwt>`.
# SSE routes (/generate, /ingest/.../stream, /chat) stream events in the response pane.

@host = http://localhost:8000
@username = admin
@password = password

### ── Health ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Public. `documentdb` flips to "down" if the DB ping fails.
GET {{host}}/health

### ── Auth ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Log in. Tagged `login` so later requests can read {{login.response.body.$.token}}.
# @name login
POST {{host}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "{{username}}",
  "password": "{{password}}"
}

### Current identity (proves the token guard works).
GET {{host}}/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.token}}

### Create a user (admin only). role is optional: "admin" | "user" (defaults to user).
POST {{host}}/auth/users
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "analyst",
  "password": "change-me",
  "role": "user"
}

### ── Foundry Local / hardware ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# Execution providers + current chat model.
GET {{host}}/hardware
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.token}}

### List catalog models (cached/loaded flags).
GET {{host}}/models
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.token}}

### Download (if needed), load, and select a chat model. Admin only.
# Accepts an alias (e.g. "qwen2.5-7b") or a full variant id (pins the execution provider).
POST {{host}}/models/select
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "model": "qwen2.5-7b-instruct-openvino-gpu:2"
}

### Stream a raw completion (SSE: token* → done | error). Sanity-checks the chat model.
POST {{host}}/generate
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "prompt": "In one sentence, what is retrieval-augmented generation?"
}

### ── Sources ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# List saved sources (any authenticated user).
GET {{host}}/sources
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.token}}

### Test a connection without saving (admin only). kind: "postgres" | "mysql" | "mssql".
# port is optional (defaults to the engine's standard port). Provide `query` OR `table`.
POST {{host}}/sources/test
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "dev-postgres",
  "kind": "postgres",
  "host": "localhost",
  "port": 5432,
  "database": "health_records",
  "username": "health",
  "password": "health",
  "table": "patient_encounters"
}

### Save a source (tests first, then stores with the password encrypted at rest).
# Admin only. Tagged `create_source` so /ingest can reuse the returned id.
# @name create_source
POST {{host}}/sources
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "dev-postgres",
  "kind": "postgres",
  "host": "localhost",
  "port": 5432,
  "database": "health_records",
  "username": "health",
  "password": "health",
  "table": "patient_encounters"
}

### ── Ingestion ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Start an ingest job (admin only). Reuses the id from the saved source above.
# `limit` is optional — cap rows for a quick trial. Returns { "job_id": ... }.
# @name ingest
POST {{host}}/ingest
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "source_id": "{{create_source.response.body.$.id}}",
  "limit": null
}

### Follow ingest progress (SSE: progress* → done | error).
GET {{host}}/ingest/{{ingest.response.body.$.job_id}}/stream
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.token}}

### ── Live logs ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Server tracing events as SSE (event: log, data: LogLine JSON). Any authenticated
# user; drops a `warn` event if a slow client falls behind. Powers the app's log
# windows. Without the Authorization header this returns 401.
GET {{host}}/logs/stream
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.token}}

### ── Retrieval + RAG chat ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Debug view of the pipeline: rewritten query, expansions, ranked/fused/reranked passages.
# mode ("vector"|"hybrid"), rerank, and top_k are optional per-request overrides.
POST {{host}}/search
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "query": "Which patient was treated for pneumonia?",
  "mode": "hybrid",
  "rerank": true,
  "top_k": 6
}

### Grounded, streamed answer with citations (SSE: citations → token* → done | error).
# `history` carries prior turns for history-aware rewrite; retrieval overrides are optional.
POST {{host}}/chat
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "question": "Which patient was treated for pneumonia, and what was prescribed?",
  "history": [],
  "mode": "hybrid",
  "rerank": true,
  "top_k": 6
}
